<b></b>INV

10:47.271 --> 10:49.021
<i>You are currently level 1.</i>

10:49.271 --> 10:51.901
<i>The negative level penalties 
have been removed,</i>

10:51.901 --> 10:54.991
<i>and the basic stat bonuses from 
"Pagma's Successor" have been applied.</i>

10:57.071 --> 10:59.911
I-I'm finally level 1!

11:03.541 --> 11:06.161
<b></b>Reputation with Smith has increased by 60.
Reputation in Bairan Village has increased by 200.

11:03.661 --> 11:06.161
<i>Your reputation with Smith
has reached max.</i>

11:07.501 --> 11:10.541
I had no idea you were so incredible!

11:11.841 --> 11:16.551
Forget that. Teach me how to 
make items I can sell for money.

11:16.551 --> 11:18.891
Yes, everything's ready.

11:18.891 --> 11:23.351
These are jaffa arrows. A small amount 
of jaffa is mixed into the steel.

11:23.351 --> 11:25.641
I'll show you the recipe.

11:26.351 --> 11:27.981
These aren't just normal arrows.

11:27.981 --> 11:30.561
They can partially ignore defense.

11:30.561 --> 11:34.781
In this area, they're a must-have 
for the Guardian of the Forest raid.

11:34.781 --> 11:35.901
To make them,

11:35.901 --> 11:39.281
you mix a small amount of jaffa into 
the melted steel and let it harden.

11:39.871 --> 11:44.541
Jaffa ore has very little oxygen 
in it, so it's easy to refine.

11:44.541 --> 11:47.251
It works well with iron ore.

11:47.251 --> 11:49.291
You know how to refine, right?

11:50.541 --> 11:52.541
All right, try it out.

11:52.541 --> 11:57.511
The ratio for jaffa ore, coke,
and limestone is 12 to 2 to 4.

11:58.181 --> 12:00.761
<i>I did some research before I logged in.</i>

12:01.221 --> 12:03.721
<i>Just because you know something 
doesn't mean you can do it.</i>

12:04.221 --> 12:08.601
<i>Which is why this class 
bonus helps so much.</i>

12:05.021 --> 12:08.851
<b>Furnace Temperature</b>

12:09.391 --> 12:13.321
<i>And since my dexterity increased,</i>

12:14.401 --> 12:16.651
<i>I don't make mistakes in anything I do.</i>

12:18.031 --> 12:19.031
<i>So...</i>

12:23.531 --> 12:24.661
What are you doing?

12:24.661 --> 12:27.041
That's just gonna make it brittle!

12:27.041 --> 12:28.661
Don't worry.

12:28.661 --> 12:31.291
I'll temper it after this.

12:32.171 --> 12:34.751
That's too much effort for a one-use item.

12:34.751 --> 12:36.671
Don't you want to make money?

12:43.261 --> 12:46.971
<i>Making something better will 
help you sell it for more.</i>

12:47.311 --> 12:51.691
<i>I've got nothing going for me, 
so this is the only way I can grow!</i>

12:58.191 --> 12:59.321
It's done!

13:02.491 --> 13:03.241
<b></b>Your understanding of <b>jaffa arrows</b>
has reached 100%

13:02.701 --> 13:03.951
<i>System guidance.</i>

